  "summary": "An artistic, literary and intellectual movement that emphasized emotion, individualism and the glorification of nature and the past.",
  "description": "Characterized by dramatic landscapes, intense emotional expression, and dramatic lighting. It emerged as a reaction against the rationalism of the Enlightenment and Industrial Revolution. Romantic artists often depicted sublime nature, historical events, and exotic subjects. The movement emphasized imagination and emotion over reason and order.",
